# Tailwind Styling

- Tailwind only. No ad-hoc CSS files or inline `style`, except unavoidable dynamic values.
- Colors come from semantic tokens defined in `src/index.css` (`@theme`): `bg-surface`, `text-ink`,
  `bg-cell-selected`, `text-cell-given`, `text-danger`... Never hex values or palette colors in components.

```tsx
// BAD
<div className="bg-[#eef2ff] text-indigo-600" />
// GOOD
<div className="bg-cell-related text-accent" />
```

- Build conditional classes with `cn()` from `@ui/lib/cn` (clsx + tailwind-merge).
- Repeated variants go in a typed map inside the component:

```tsx
const VARIANT_CLASSES: Record<ButtonVariant, string> = { primary: '...', ghost: '...' }
```

- Dark mode: tokens switch under the `.dark` class; components rarely need `dark:`.
- Touch targets: controls are at least 44px (`min-h-11 min-w-11`). Board cells are the documented exception.
- Respect reduced motion: animations use `motion-safe:`.
